    "title": "Get Well Soon Flowers for Hospital Delivery in Nairobi: What to Send and What to Avoid",
    "excerpt": "Visiting a patient or sending cheer from afar? A Nairobi guide to get-well flowers and fruit baskets — hospital-friendly choices, scent tips, timing and same-day delivery.",
    "content": "<p><em>Last updated: 18 October 2026</em> · By The Stems Flowers, Nairobi</p>\n\n<p><strong>Get well soon flowers in Nairobi should be gentle, easy to place beside a bed, and respectful of hospital rules.</strong> People searching “get well flowers hospital Nairobi”, “flowers for patient Kenya”, “fruit basket hospital delivery” or “cheer up bouquet Westlands hospital” are usually colleagues, church mates, relatives or diaspora family who want to show up without causing nurses a problem. This guide covers what to send, what to skip, and how delivery works.</p>\n\n<h2>Who is ordering — and what do they worry about?</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li>Office teams collecting money for a colleague in Nairobi Hospital, Aga Khan, MP Shah or Kenyatta</li>\n  <li>Family sending love when they cannot all visit at once</li>\n  <li>Friends who want colour without heavy perfume in a shared ward</li>\n  <li>Relatives abroad who only have a ward name and a phone number</li>\n</ul>\n<p>What they consider: Is scent too strong? Will security allow flowers? Is a fruit basket more practical than blooms? Can it arrive during visiting hours?</p>\n\n<h2>Are flowers allowed in Nairobi hospitals?</h2>\n<p>Many private hospitals allow modest bouquets during visiting hours; some wards (ICU, high dependency, neonatal) restrict flowers. Always:</p>\n<ol>\n  <li>Ask the family or hospital desk when unsure</li>\n  <li>Prefer compact arrangements over huge standing sprays</li>\n  <li>Include the ward, patient full name and a reachable mobile</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Best get-well flower choices</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Why it works</th><th>Typical budget</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Soft mixed / pastel bouquet</td><td>Cheerful without heavy romance</td><td>KES 3,000–3,500</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Gentle pink or white tones</td><td>Calm, respectful</td><td>KES 3,500–4,500</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Fruit basket</td><td>Practical for recovery; often loved by nurses’ advice</td><td>See <a href=\"/fruit-baskets-nairobi\">fruit baskets</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Small bouquet + card only</td><td>Fits crowded bedside tables</td><td>KES 3,000+</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Browse <a href=\"/get-well-soon-flowers-nairobi\">get well soon flowers Nairobi</a> and avoid overpowering scented designs unless the family requests them.</p>\n\n<h2>What to avoid sending to a hospital</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li>Very large floor arrangements that block walkways</li>\n  <li>Strongly scented blooms in shared wards</li>\n  <li>Balloons where hospitals ban them</li>\n  <li>Food hampers with alcohol unless the family confirms</li>\n  <li>Surprise deliveries to ICU without family approval</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Card messages that feel caring (not awkward)</h2>\n<ol>\n  <li>“Rest well. We are praying for a quick recovery.”</li>\n  <li>“Thinking of you — the office sends love.”</li>\n  <li>“Take every day gently. We are here when you need us.”</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>How hospital delivery works with The Stems</h2>\n<p>Share patient name, hospital, ward/room if known, visitor rules, and a family contact number. We deliver across Nairobi same day when you order by <strong>4PM</strong>. For estates after discharge, we can redirect to Westlands, Kileleshwa, Karen or CBD homes — see <a href=\"/blog/flower-delivery-nairobi\">delivery guide</a>.</p>\n\n<h2>Office collections: how to organise a group gift</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li>Pick one budget owner and one WhatsApp thread</li>\n  <li>Choose a mid-range bouquet (KES 3,500–5,500) or fruit basket so contributions stay fair</li>\n  <li>Sign the card with the team name, not 25 micro-messages</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<p><strong>What flowers are best for get well soon in Kenya?</strong><br />Soft mixed pastels or gentle pinks — bright enough to cheer, calm enough for a ward.</p>\n<p><strong>Should I send a fruit basket instead of flowers?</strong><br />Often yes for longer stays. Many families appreciate both a small bouquet and fruit.</p>\n<p><strong>Can you deliver to Nairobi Hospital / Aga Khan / MP Shah?</strong><br />Yes when visiting rules allow — send us the hospital and ward details on WhatsApp.</p>\n<p><strong>How much should a workplace spend?</strong><br />KES 3,500–8,500 covers most thoughtful team gifts including a simple hamper upgrade.</p>\n<p><strong>Can diaspora family send get-well gifts to Nairobi?</strong><br />Yes — <a href=\"/blog/send-flowers-to-kenya-from-abroad\">send flowers to Kenya from abroad</a>.</p>\n\n<p class=\"not-prose\"><a href=\"https://wa.me/254725707143?text=Hello!%20I'd%20like%20get-well%20flowers%20or%20a%20fruit%20basket%20delivered%20to%20a%20hospital%20in%20Nairobi.\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:#25D366;color:#fff;font-weight:600;padding:0.75rem 1.25rem;border-radius:0.5rem;text-decoration:none;\">Order on WhatsApp</a></p>\n<p>Related: <a href=\"/get-well-soon-flowers-nairobi\">Get well flowers</a> · <a href=\"/fruit-baskets-nairobi\">Fruit baskets</a> · <a href=\"/blog/what-flowers-to-send-occasion-kenya\">Occasion guide</a></p>",
